tests/ui/check/ok_cost_proven.sky:2:5: note: cost of `gram`: 2·M²·N flops, 2 allocations (M·N + M² floats in all)
  |
2 | def gram(A: Matrix[N, M]) -> Matrix[M, M]:
  |     ^^^^
4 |     return Aᵀ @ A
  |            -- hot spot: `Aᵀ` costs 16·M·N bytes of memory traffic
  |            ------ hot spot: `Aᵀ @ A` costs 2·M²·N flops
  = note: memory traffic: 24·M·N bytes read, 8·M·N + 8·M² bytes written

tests/ui/check/ok_cost_proven.sky:3:5: note: `gram` costs 2·M²·N flops, within `2 * N * M^2`
  |
3 |     cost flops <= 2 * N * M^2
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = note: proven from the static cost model, for every size from 1 up
  = note: the cost is that of the optimized program (spec "Performance contracts")

tests/ui/check/ok_cost_proven.sky:6:5: note: cost of `step`: 2·N flops, 1 allocation of N floats
